  "key_findings_summary": [
    "1. 153,351 cleaned instruction samples from 8 specialized pipelines (211K raw, 27.4% rejection)",
    "2. Vendi Score = 182.75 on 15K sample; scaling law: V(N) = 55.4(1-e^(-N/745)) + 109.0, R\u00b2=0.996",
    "3. Self-Inversion is the most valuable pipeline per sample: 25.1 Vendi/1K (12\u00d7 Complex QA)",
    "4. 2,274 exclusive domains from Self-Inversion (143\u00d7 more than any other pipeline)",
    "5. K-Center-Greedy selection: +33% diversity at N=500",
    "6. Random selection near-optimal at N>5000 (<2% gap)",
    "7. Just 2 sources (Self-Inv + Doc QA) achieve 96% of maximum Vendi Score",
    "8. Document QA most valuable by leave-one-out: +6.2% when removed",
    "9. Creative Writing redundant: -3.2% Vendi when removed (helps to remove it)",
    "10. Optimal mixing: upweight Self-Inv 3.2%\u219217.4%, downweight Complex QA 35.4%\u219213.7%",
    "11. No benchmark contamination: 0 matches across MMLU, GSM8K, HumanEval, ARC, HellaSwag",
    "12. Cost: $2,245 total ($15.58/1K clean samples)",
    "13. High intrinsic dimensionality: >100 PCA components for 90% variance",
    "14. Clear pipeline complementarity: within-source sim 0.135 vs between-source 0.038",
    "15. Multi-turn quality maintained: TTR stable at 0.84-0.85 across turn depths"
  ]
